    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d880">

                <pb facs="1027" n="947" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg947"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Crown Prince of Siam to President
                    Roosevelt.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Sumas, Wash.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-11-30"><hi rendition="#italic">November 30,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Having completed a most interesting tour through the United States, I now beg to
                    take leave of Your Excellency, and to express my heartiest appreciation and
                    gratitude for the very hospitable reception so kindly accorded to me by you and
                    by the officials and the citizens of this friendly country. I assure you that I
                    bear home with me the happiest memories of America and the Americans.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Maha Vajiravudh.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
